  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: oauthlib 3.3.0+rhlw.1",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released oauthlib 3.3.0+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-49272, CVE-2026-49264, and CVE-2026-49265.\n\nCVE-2026-49272: OAuthLib: Bearer token can be retrieved as long as client knows a valid client ID for device workflow\n\nCVE-2026-49264: OAuthLib: Unsafe JSONP callback injection in RevocationEndpoint allows arbitrary JavaScript response generation\n\nCVE-2026-49265: OAuthLib: Timing Attack Vulnerability in PKCE code_verifier Comparison\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for oauthlib 3.3.0 from PyPI.",
